          with a development server running. The built console is a single
          file of roughly 250&nbsp;KB.
        </p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem">
          Run <code style="background:#E4F0F9;padding:.1rem .35rem">npm run build:single</code>
          and upload the <code style="background:#E4F0F9;padding:.1rem .35rem">dist/index.html</code>
          it writes, replacing this file.
        </p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#51626F;font-size:14px">
          Both files are called <code>index.html</code>, which is how this one
          ends up published by mistake. Uploading the source folder to the same
          repository as the site will do it every time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.tsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>

